# FS-01 — Opportunity Runtime Stabilization

**Status:** Implementation Complete · Ready for Business Acceptance Testing · Awaiting Product Owner Certification  

Do **not** treat as FOUNDATION CERTIFIED or FROZEN until the Product Owner explicitly confirms **"FS-01 Approved"** after BAT on the latest production deployment.

## Constitutional principle

The **Opportunity Registry** is the **only** runtime authority for the Opportunity lifecycle.

LoanFile must **not** be required to execute:

- Opportunity Workspace / Header / Timeline
- Document Center
- Credit Bench (Lead Creation)
- Credit Workbench
- LIFE

LoanFile may remain only as a **temporary compatibility layer** (Deal attachment). It must never behave as the runtime source of truth.

## Expected runtime

Contact → Opportunity Service → Opportunity Registry → Shared Opportunity Context → Opportunity Workspace → Document Center → Credit Bench → LIFE

## Shared Opportunity Context

SSOT session context: `src/lib/lead-opportunity-journey/active-context.ts`

Stages resolve via `useOpportunityWorkspaceContext` / `rememberOpportunityRegistryContext`.

`fileId` is optional Deal attachment only — never equal to `opportunityId`.

## Runtime adapter

Canonical resolve: `src/lib/lead-opportunity-journey/opportunity-runtime-adapter.ts`

Governed by **CAD-2026-001** (Business Data Provenance) — see `.cursor/rules/business-data-provenance-cad-2026-001.mdc` and ADR-017.

- `resolveOpportunityRuntimeCase` (async) — stages must use this
- Projects Opportunity → LoanFile-shaped **structure** only (`__fs01OpportunityRuntime`)
- **Never** invents business values (`secured` / `fresh` / amounts / `medium` priority / placeholder customer names). Uncaptured → UI **Not Specified**
- Optionally remembers linked legacy LoanFile id on context — never overlays LoanFile business fields into OW
- Field provenance: `docs/co-arch-003/CO-ARCH-OPPORTUNITY-FIELD-PROVENANCE.md`

Do not call `loadLoanFiles` / Deal DAL to decide which Opportunity is open or what business values to show.

## Documents

Document Registry links prefer `opportunityId`. Do not dual-write Deal when runtime is Opportunity-only.

## Prohibited

- Hard-gating Opportunity stages on LoanFile presence
- Picking an unrelated open LoanFile for LIFE / journey context
- Writing Opportunity planning state into LoanFile storage as SSOT
- Marking FS-01 FOUNDATION CERTIFIED / FROZEN before Product Owner **"FS-01 Approved"**
- Implementing FS-02 Deal transition work under FS-01
